  <content>
  <note class="self-check"><para>Terence looked down the second column of the table below and noticed that \(\frac{3}{1}=\frac{9}{3}=\frac{27}{9}=\frac{81}{27}\). Because of his observation, he claimed that the input-output pairs in this table could be modeled with an exponential function. Explain why Terence is correct or incorrect.</para>
<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
  <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        \(x\)
     </emphasis> </entry><entry><emphasis>
        \(T(x)\)
     </emphasis> </entry></row>
  <row>
      <entry>
        0
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
      <entry>
        9
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        13
      </entry>
      <entry>
        27
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        40
      </entry>
      <entry>
        81
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>
</note>
</content>
</document>